      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T23:22:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that @joshuaduong@google.com is already looking into fixing up the boxed handle system to handle duplicated unboxed handles and given that this change already adds custom boxed/unboxed handling of `VkQueue`, what if we just (ab)used duplicated unboxed handles right now?\n\nYou could just do a single \n\n```\nVALIDATE_NEW_HANDLE_INFO_ENTRY(mQueueInfo, physicalQueue);\nQueueInfo\u0026 physicalQueueInfo \u003d mQueueInfo[physicalQueue];\n```\n\nwith the single unboxed-`VkQueue`, you could generate 2 boxed-`VkQueue` with two calls to `new_boxed_VkQueue()` calls which both point at the same unboxed-`VkQueue`, and then you could update the custom `unboxed_to_boxed_VkQueue()` implementation to just do an `GFXSTREAM_ABORT() \u003c\u003c \"Never call this function.\"` since it is never used anyway. \n\nYou might have to add a `std::vector\u003cVkQueue\u003e boxedQueues;` to `DeviceInfo` so that we clean up both boxed handles during `vkDestroyDevice()`.\n\nI think this would allow you to remove almost all of the new custom boxed/unboxed handling from this change except for making the `unboxed_to_boxed_VkQueue()` an abort.\n\nWDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2160,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2169,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "eeccf5f8bb867ac5f85b5e8a8aadfcba2b7fdc63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b778ff51_47d669c0",
        "filename": "host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 2169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1967833
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T13:55:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if I get this right, but calling `new_boxed_VkQueue` right now requires unique unboxed handles, so cannot be done twice with the same handle.  I think a layer to create unique handles is not directly related to this change, and we should be getting unique dispatchable handles right now anyway.\n\nI believe `boxed_to_boxed_VkQueue` is not necessary and I\u0027ve actually removed it with this CL. I think raw unboxed handles should not be converted back to boxed ones even if we have a layer to make them unique. Using higher level mQueueInfo or similar structures would be better for such operations, given that we always get the unboxed handle via an unboxing operation. If we start reading back handles from GPU directly for any reasons, that\u0027d be another story.",
      "parentUuid": "d5a2a616_56cfec1b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2160,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2169,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "eeccf5f8bb867ac5f85b5e8a8aadfcba2b7fdc63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f31ed9bd_63d44e1d",
        "filename": "host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 2169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561731
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T16:43:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding was that it was only the `m[VkType]Info` maps that needed the unique unboxed handles (because you can\u0027t have 2 infos for the same host handle) and that `new_boxed_[VkType]` may only want unique unboxed handles for the reverse map in order to support `unboxed_to_boxed_[VkType]` but this is never used for `VkQueue`.",
      "parentUuid": "b778ff51_47d669c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2160,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2169,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "eeccf5f8bb867ac5f85b5e8a8aadfcba2b7fdc63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
