      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T14:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess I am just trying to avoid unexpected behavior where off the cuff we advertise we support 2 queues and someone is trying to use the case I described above, but then we crash because we sneakily set the second queue to be part of the same family as the first one. So maybe a log, comment or an ERR if the second queue is different from the first could mitigate this for now and in the future give us good errors if we encounter this case?",
      "parentUuid": "a19c5bd0_8b9b21a6",
      "revId": "eeccf5f8bb867ac5f85b5e8a8aadfcba2b7fdc63",
